# Required tools

This is the normative tool inventory for BigQuery Analytics. Installation and
verification missions must read this file rather than inventing tool names,
paths, or installation methods.

## Shared rules

- Probe a user-supplied path first, then the bare command on `PATH`, then the
  canonical install path only to diagnose an incomplete installation.
- Installation requires structured user consent.
- macOS and Linux use the official Google Cloud SDK archive under
  `~/google-cloud-sdk`; expose `gcloud` and `bq` through non-destructive symlinks
  under `~/bin`.
- Windows uses the official Google Cloud SDK installer/default local path.
- `bq` ships with the Google Cloud SDK. Never perform a second SDK installation
  merely because `bq` is missing; repair/install the shared SDK once.
- Resolve extensions against the installed **Sedea** application, not another
  editor profile.

## Tool inventory

### `gcloud`

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| `id` | `gcloud` |
| `kind` | `cli` |
| `cli` | `gcloud` |
| `minVersion` | `450.0.0` |
| `docsUrl` | https://cloud.google.com/sdk/gcloud |
| `installUrl` | https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install-sdk |
| `macosInstallPath` | `~/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud` |
| `linuxInstallPath` | `~/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud` |
| `windowsInstallPath` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Google\CloudSDK\google-cloud-sdk\bin\gcloud.cmd` |
| `macosMethods` | `curl-sdk` |
| `linuxMethods` | `curl-sdk` |
| `windowsMethods` | `official-sdk-installer` |

Dry-runs:

1. `gcloud version` — exit 0 and version ≥ `450.0.0`.
2. `gcloud help` — exit 0.

### `bq`

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| `id` | `bq` |
| `kind` | `cli` |
